\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Which configurations agree on every edge?}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{The sign field and its flip contribute equally at zero external
field. Their common weight still depends on whether neighboring
signs agree. For the three-position clock the cost of a disagreement
is different. How does the distance between the endpoint values
determine the loss of weight on the whole graph?}
